8619903,2024-03-26,Credit card,Store credit card,Closing your account,Can't close your account,"I am filing this complaint because my Victoria 's Secret store card was closed. When I called to inquire about the reason for the closure, the representative informed me that it was closed due to inactivity. I asked if she could reopen my account, to which she responded that she would not be able to do so without pulling my credit again. Therefore, according to CFR Part 1026.11 ( 2 ) ( B ) states : "" Nothing in paragraph ( b ) ( 1 ) of this section prohibits a creditor from terminating an account that is inactive for three or more consecutive months. An account is inactive for purposes of this paragraph if no credit has been extended ( such as by purchase, cash advance, or balance transfer ) and if the account has no outstanding balance. '' This implies that they should not have closed my account due to inactivity. Additionally, by informing me of the closure, they are still selling my security, which was generated when I filled out the application, as applications can be transferred to third parties. This process securitizes the application, allowing them to sell it on both primary and secondary markets. 
